 "▼ Dive in: <0>Stages</0>": "",
 "RAG has two phases: <0>index</0> (offline: load → split → embed → store) and <1>query</1> (online: embed question → top-k search → stuff chunks into the prompt → LLM answers).": "",
 "LangChain provides one component per box: <0/>, an <1/> class, a vector store such as <2/>, <3/> and <4/>.": "",
 "The model never \"searches\": retrieved text simply becomes more tokens in the prompt (see <0>RAG pipeline</0>).": "",
 "FAISS is an in-process similarity-search library; any other vector store exposes the same retriever interface, so the chain does not change.": "",
 "Embedding the query and the chunks must use the <0>same</0> embedding model.": "",
