 "Deepest level reached — next slide → <0>Production tips: sizing, metadata, evaluation, re-indexing, hybrid search</0>": "",
 "Checklist": "",
 "Eval demo": "",
 "Chunk sizing": "",
 "Start around a few hundred tokens with {#}–{#}% overlap (a common starting point, not a rule); try structure-aware splits (headings, code blocks).": "",
 "Metadata filters": "",
 "Filter by source, date, tenant or permissions <0>before</0> ranking. Never rely on the prompt to enforce access control.": "",
 "Evaluation": "",
 "Build a small question → expected-chunk set; track recall@k and answer quality when you change anything.": "",
 "Re-indexing": "",
 "Version your index; re-embed when the embedding model or chunking changes. Do not mix vectors from different models.": "",
 "Hybrid search": "",
 "Blend keyword (BM25) and vector scores; add a reranker for the top ~{#}. Helps with IDs, names and rare terms.": "",
 "Go deeper: <0>hybrid search, reranking, agentic RAG</0> and <1>evals</1>.": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Checklist</0>": "",
 "Most RAG failures are <0>retrieval</0> failures (right chunk not retrieved), not generation failures — measure retrieval separately.": "",
 "Tune chunk size and overlap on <0>your</0> documents and questions; there is no universal best value.": "",
 "Combine vector search with keyword search, metadata filters and reranking when exact terms or scoping matter (see <0>advanced RAG</0>).": "",
 "Store metadata (source, section, date, access rights) with each chunk; filter before similarity search where the store supports it.": "",
 "Plan re-indexing: changing the embedding model, the chunking, or the documents requires rebuilding or incrementally updating the index; keep an index version.": "",
